// expect: refuse E_PatternInexhaustive
// A literal inside a constructor's payload covers one value of a word, never
// the word: `Some(false)` leaves `Some(true)` to no arm. On boot 82692525 the
// exhaustiveness matrix read a literal column as covered, so this compiled
// clean and trapped at the match (exit 134) when `Some(true)` arrived; the
// strict matrix refuses it, naming the value no arm takes.
fn pick(o) = match o {
  Some(false) => 1,
  None => 2,
}

fn main() = pick(Some(true))
